Package: azan-sip-client
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: AthanBox <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Fudgeamin99/azan-sip-box
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), cage, xwayland, seatd, chromium, libgl1-mesa-dri, fonts-dejavu-core, alsa-utils, dbus, libpam-systemd, iproute2, libnss-mdns, wayland-utils, ca-certificates
Recommends: avahi-daemon, alsa-ucm-conf, firmware-intel-sound, wlopm, wlr-randr, iw, wpasupplicant
Description: AthanBox prayer times and azan on a TV, a Wyse or a laptop
 Turns a small Debian computer, such as a Dell Wyse thin client or an old
 laptop, 64-bit or 32-bit, into a TV screen for AthanBox. It shows
 AthanBox's prayer-times screen full screen on the TV plugged into it (or the
 laptop's own screen), from every boot, and plays the azan through the TV's
 speakers (or the laptop's) at the same moment as the phones, at a volume
 of its own. With two screens or more, each one shows the prayer times.
 It finds AthanBox on the network, reconnects by itself after AthanBox
 restarts or the network drops, and updates itself from Screen settings.
